  "term": "fuzzy logic",
  "definition": "Fuzzy logic is a way of reasoning with approximate, quantitative judgments when language is ambiguous rather than strictly precise. It uses everyday terms like good, bad, or young, along with qualifiers like more, less, and very, as flexible categories within a given problem.",
